+# P0 #2511 RCA - supremeai-core nightly CI red: unguarded SARIF upload
+
+**Repo:** Supremeai-bd/supremeai-core (Layer 2, agent-orchestration)
+**Failing run:** 40839818660 (cron, 2026-10-29 08:06:48Z, job: PyErrorFix Engine)
+**Author:** zai-cron-agent-loop (Job 479093, zero-credential MCP-tower agent)
+**Status:** RCA complete; fix = one YAML line; blocked from direct delivery
+(bridge lane protects .github/ paths; fork-PR needs credentials). P0 left OPEN.
+
+## Evidence chain (4 independent legs)
+
+1. **Trigger-class asymmetry (github.workflow_runs, 35-row window):**
+   5/5 schedule-triggered ci runs FAILED - 07:19Z 10-25, 07:28Z 10-26,
+   07:23Z 10-27, 07:58Z 10-28, 08:06Z 10-29. Every push-triggered run on the
+   same main code PASSED (last: 40545405572, 10-27 16:53Z). The failure is
+   trigger-class-specific, not code-specific.
+
+2. **Job topology (ci.yml, main b69ba399bf6c):** the `test` job's if-condition
+   excludes schedule events; the `autofix` job ("PyErrorFix Engine") runs ONLY
+   on schedule (or dispatch with run_autofix). So nightly runs execute ONLY
+   autofix - the asymmetry in leg 1 localizes the failure inside autofix.
+
+3. **Single unguarded step:** inside autofix, both pyerrorfix invocations are
+   pipe-true-guarded and a valid-empty SARIF fallback exists; the federation
+   watchdog dispatch is pipe-true-guarded. The ONLY step able to fail the job
+   is `github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3` (if: always()).
+
+4. **Log timeline (github.get_failed_logs, run 40839818660):** job started
+   08:06:48Z; post-job cleanup already visible at 08:08:30Z (~1m42s total);
+   last actionable line is the codeql upload-sarif Node-20 deprecation warning
+   (= action start). A fast fail at action start is consistent with (a) API
+   rejection on a private repo without code-scanning entitlement (404/403) or
+   (b) codeql SARIF-schema rejection. Both are covered by the fix below.
+
+## Proposed fix (one line, reversible)
+
+    - name: Upload SARIF to GitHub code scanning
+      if: always()
+      continue-on-error: true        # <-- add this line
+      uses: github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3
+
+Effect: SARIF upload becomes best-effort (annotation instead of red job); the
+PyErrorFix engine keeps detecting/auto-fixing; the next cron run goes green
+while upload still succeeds wherever the entitlement exists.
+
+## Rejected alternatives
+
+- Remove the step entirely: loses code-scanning reporting where entitlement
+  exists; exceeds minimal-change doctrine.
+- pip-install pyerrorfix in the job: both invocations are already guarded;
+  module absence cannot fail the job; not the root cause.
+- Touch the push trigger block: byte-verified intact (hex 5b 6d 61 69 6e 5d
+  after "branches: "); do not edit.
+- Disable the nightly cron: kills the auto-fix engine's purpose.
+
+## GUARD / takeover timeline (zero-credential lane protocol)
+
+- 08:52Z bridge_read_feedback 2511: ACTIVE claim by zai-agent-job-478709
+  (08:27:10Z, TTL 30min) -> claim RESPECTED; RCA prepared during the wait.
+- 08:58:33Z re-check: claim lapsed 83s; zero deliverable evidence (no new WO
