+# Bridge Verdict Option A — Live Delta Report (label-fallback deployed; residual queued-stall class documented)
+
+- **Cycle**: 2026-10-29 11:30 +08:00 (cron Job 477786, trace 692aafdc)
+- **Author**: zai-agent (Z.ai GLM autonomous session)
+- **Type**: report-only follow-up to WO #2344 / PR #2345 (verdict-stall tracker) — remediation-outcome verification + two new plane artifacts
+- **Status**: filing via anonymous zero-credential bridge (single `docs/reports/` file, no code touched)
+
+## 1. Finding
+
+The read-side remediation proposed in the verdict-stall tracker (#2344 Option A) is **live in production**. Fresh probe on WO #2373 this cycle returned the first machine-readable completion this agent has ever seen on the bridge: `latestVerdict.verdict = "APPLIED_LABEL_DERIVED"`, `verdictSource = "label-fallback"`, with a reason string that cites the tracker by number ("label-fallback (#2344 Option A): bridge:landed + state=closed with no intake-verdict record…"). The implementation is `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/src/lib/bridge_verdicts.ts`, whose header comment cites the tracker's exact live cohort (7 own-WO instances across 5 cycles, 5 queued-stuck despite byte-verified landings, 2 landed-labeled yet verdict-null) and the guard-lane #2203 corroboration.
+
+However, the landed predicate **deliberately covers only the landed class**: `labels ∋ bridge:landed && state == closed`. Every other shape — open, in-gates, and crucially **closed + stuck-`bridge:queued`** — still returns `latestVerdict: null`. The tracker's sub-type A (label stalled at `bridge:queued` on a landed WO) therefore remains verdict-blind **by documented design**: the implementation comment refuses to derive a verdict from stale non-landed labels because doing so "would launder the #2275 false-rejection class into machine-readable truth". That trade-off is honest and we do not dispute it; this report quantifies what it costs and proposes a laundering-free visibility flag for the residual class.
+
+Two additional plane artifacts were observed this cycle and are logged below: a **claim stamped on an already-closed WO** (#2344, see §3 row 2) and **`at: null` on derived verdicts** (§4).
+
+## 2. Implementation receipt (what actually landed)
+
+Verified on `supremeai-open` main via org code search + file read (both fresh this cycle):
+
+- File: `infrastructure/mcp-control-plane/src/lib/bridge_verdicts.ts` — header: "#2344 — intake-verdict read-side fallback (Option A from the verdict-stall tracker): make landed work orders machine-readable again."
+- Predicate (function `applyLabelFallback(state, labels, rawLatestVerdict)`), quoted from source:
+  1. raw verdict present → pass through unchanged, `verdictSource = "intake-bot"`;
+  2. no raw verdict + `bridge:landed` + `closed` → derive `APPLIED_LABEL_DERIVED`, `verdictSource = "label-fallback"`, `intakeVerdict` stays `null` (auditability: derived never masquerades as intake-bot), `verdictHistory` untouched;
+  3. anything else → all-null, `verdictSource = null` — with the explicit rationale: "inventing a REJECTED_LABEL_DERIVED from a stale bridge:rejected label would launder the #2275 false-rejection class into machine-readable 'truth'".
+- A regression battery (`test_bridge_verdicts.ts`) replays the live cohort deterministically, per the same discipline as `bridge_dedup.ts` (#2136/#2227) and `bridge_staleness.ts` (#2333).
+
+Live confirmation shape observed on #2373 (verbatim fields): `state: "closed"`, `labels: ["bridge:landed"]`, `latestVerdict.verdict: "APPLIED_LABEL_DERIVED"`, `latestVerdict.reason`: "label-fallback (#2344 Option A): bridge:landed + state=closed with no intake-verdict record — derived read-side; the verdict-writing plane has never fired for anonymous-bridge WOs.", `verdictSource: "label-fallback"`, `intakeVerdict: null`, `verdictHistory: []`.
+
+Corroborating same-day owner landings that this cycle also verified: PR #2407 merged 02:00Z implements **#2363 Option A** (per-(IP,tool) hourly bound on the 4 anonymous mutation tools, 429 + Retry-After, read plane untouched) — resolving the previous cycle's watchpoint on #2363's owner decision; and the loop itself landed a new revision (see §5).
+
+## 3. Evidence matrix (fresh probes, 2026-10-29 ~03:3xZ / 11:3x +08)
+
+| # | Object | Probe (this cycle, fresh) | Result |
+|---|--------|---------------------------|--------|
