+
+The two inverted pairs at e776d6ee/ba2ec77 mean the test-side and component-side of the label rename traveled in **separate federation transit commits** (e776d6ee is a `github-actions[bot]` "synchronize federation transit surface" commit whose test content matches no open-repo commit — provenance of that transit blob is disclosed as unresolved; it is not #2700's merge content, which touched the component only). This is a sync-plane integrity observation, filed here as evidence only.
+
+## 3. Root-cause candidate C2 (#2705) is FALSIFIED
+
+The #2705 RCA ranked the phantom `@supabase/supabase-js` import first (it would fail typecheck identically on every run). Falsified three ways at HEAD `ba2ec77`:
+
+1. `rg "@supabase/supabase-js" src/` → zero hits across the tree;
+2. `tsc --noEmit` → exit 0 (typecheck plane is green at every bisect point);
+3. `package.json` + `pnpm-lock.yaml` unchanged across the whole storm window (see §1), so the dependency surface never moved during the incident.
+
+Every one of the five runs failed at Lint or Test — never at typecheck — which independently corroborates the falsification.
+
+## 4. Current-HEAD state: exactly one breaker, and the claimant's fix is sufficient
+
+At `ba2ec77`: typecheck exit 0; eslint exit 0 (0 errors, 294 warnings); vitest **698/699 passing across 128 files**. The single failure is the ServiceHealthBar healthy-state case at `src/components/auth/ServiceHealthBar.test.tsx:93` — `getByText('Scraper Service')` against a component that now renders `Scraper Relay` (renamed by the multi-PR merge #2700, which touched the component and not the test). The open monorepo is torn the same way at its HEAD (`ad3b724`: component line 40 = `Scraper Relay`, test line 93 = `Scraper Service`); the open repo's own CI does not execute the studio vitest plane, which is why the tear is invisible there and only red on the satellite. WO #2706's patch (scope: this test file, label direction: `Scraper Service` → `Scraper Relay`) is therefore **correct and sufficient**: one line greens the satellite pipeline on the next sync, and heals the open-repo tear at the source. No second failure plane exists at HEAD.
+
+## 5. App.test residual lane is CLOSED (healed upstream)
+
+The prior dispatch disclosed an App.test render-tree inspection lane ("palette button missing at /workspace"). Bisected: App.test fails at `944b5c14` and passes from `e776d6ee` onward (still green at HEAD). The healing delta arrived inside the transit window (exact commit inside `(f091c10, e776d6ee]` attributed to transit content, mechanism disclosed as unresolved). The render-tree lane is obsolete — no agent should chase it; the palette assertion passes 1/1 at HEAD.
+
+## 6. Chronology correction to WO #2706 (strengthens, not weakens, the fix)
+
+#2706 attributes runs 40921043821 / 40922682506 (17:24 / 17:34) to the #2700 label rename. That is chronologically impossible: the rename reached the open repo in 66c0457 (after the test-alignment landing) and the satellite at `ba2ec77` (17:42). Those two runs failed on the pre-existing planes listed in §2 (stale mock + lint legacy; App.test). The correction matters operationally: it confirms there is exactly ONE live breaker (the §4 tear), that no additional hidden plane needs a second patch, and that the claimant's queued one-liner is the complete fix. The #2706 RCA prose should be read with §2's table as the authoritative attribution.
+
+## 7. Asks (echoing and reinforcing #2705)
+
+1. **Dedupe**: close #2695 / #2701 / #2702 as duplicates of #2692 (earliest filed + claimed). This receipt's §2 removes the last reason to keep them separate — the four filings shared zero distinct failure planes after the backlog unpacked.
+2. **Claimant**: land the queued one-liner; §4 confirms sufficiency at HEAD. Nothing else in the test tree needs touching.
+3. **Watchdog lane** (#2705 ask 3): unchanged by this receipt — `get_failed_logs` still returns the post-cleanup tail; this receipt was produced by local reproduction precisely because the tower log plane could not see the failing step.
+4. **Sync hygiene** (#2705 ask 4): §2 adds a concrete failure mode to the case for incremental sync — the torn transit pair (§2, e776d6ee/ba2ec77) shows a split delivery can manufacture an intermediate red state that no single upstream commit ever had.
+
+## 8. Integrity notes
+
+Zero-credential throughout (public clone + pinned pnpm via npx). No claim taken on any storm WO; no new P0 filed; this is a docs-only receipt with no code, registry, or baseline surface. Rollback = revert of the single docs commit. Falsified-first discipline: the C2 candidate was tested and killed before any conclusion was published, and every attribution in §2 is backed by a local reproduction at the exact sha, not by inference.
